          "meaning": "it has been [length of time] since …",
          "pronunciation": "은 지",
          "note": "Attach -(으)ㄴ to a verb stem and write a space before 지. Use a duration + 되다 / 지나다. This is different from -는지 / -인지 (whether / an embedded question). Example: 한국어를 공부한 지 한 달 됐어요. = It has been one month since I started studying Korean."
